## Purpose
- Keep agent changes small, verifiable, and consistent with project practices.

## Source of truth
- Existing code layout in `services/`, `frontend/`, `docker-compose.yml`
- Existing tests in `services/team-hub-auth/team-hub-auth.Tests`

## Do
- Make minimal scoped changes; keep unrelated files untouched.
- Prefer config-driven values (`appsettings*.json`, env vars) over hardcoded constants.
- Add/adjust tests with behavior changes (especially auth endpoints and token logic).
- Keep naming consistent with existing route/config ids (`auth-cluster`, `/api/auth/*`).
- Validate docs/code consistency after edits (paths, ports, endpoint names).

## Don't
- Do not use destructive git commands.
- Do not introduce "magic" URLs/ports outside config.
- Do not change public API contract silently.
- Do not add verbose comments where code is already clear.

## Checklist
- Scope limited to requested files.
- Behavior changes are testable and tested when relevant.
- Commit/PR messages should explain why, not only what.
